  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Lash Whip" id="6a1e-635c-1bed-ca7f" hidden="false" page="52" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>At the start of close combat phase a model with a lash whip can make 3 attacks against enemy models in base contact. These can be made at separate targets or all against the same one. A model that is attacked has to roll a D6 and get under it&apos;s Initiative characteristic to avoid the attack. 
Once the lash whip attacks are resolved continue the fight as normal. The model with the lash whip can still fight as normal but does not count the lash whip as an additional close combat weapon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Spinefist" id="691c-d4b5-7686-867f" hidden="false" page="53" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Uses middle sized Flamer template. Make a to hit roll against every target that is at least half under the template, taking into account any modifiers as normal for cover/movement etc. 
If the Spinefist is used in close combat the template is not used. It only hits the target you choose.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Strangleweb" id="a4a8-bf16-a229-fd25" hidden="false" page="53" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Uses Hand Flamer template
Any models completely under are automatically hit. Any partials are hit on a 4+
Roll a D6 and add the models hit Strength to the roll. If the total is 9 or more the mode brekas free of the web. Otherwise make an armour save. If failed suffers 1 wound.
Force fields cannot be used, but shields can (like Storm Shields). 
Models that are trapped in the web can try and break free again at the start of its next turn and each thereafter until they break free or die.
Any entrapped model may not do anything except use psychic powers if it has any. Vehicles cannot be affected by the Strangelweb, but exposed c rew or passengers can be hit and trapped.
See Codex Pg. 53 for further rules</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Deathspitter" id="90b8-357f-537c-d17d" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>If a Deathspitter scores a hit on an enemy model other models nearby may also be hit. Roll a D6 for any models within 2&quot; of the model hit by the Deathspitter. On a roll of 4+ they suffer a S3 hit with no save modifiers. The Deathspitter doesn&apos;t have to Wound the target before you check for splatter, only a hit is needed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flamespurt" id="e1ec-dbda-798c-a323" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Uses medium sized flamer template.
Any models under are automatically hit, any partial are hit on a 4+
Any models not slain must be moved to the templates edge. If a model cannot move out of th eway for any reason they suffer a second hit, but no further.
Vehicles, Terminators or anything with a Toughness of 7 or higher will not be moved as they are too well protected</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flesh Hooks" id="bb9d-62e0-ac60-d702" hidden="false" page="55" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>If a model survives a hit from a flesh hook it is snagged by the hook and dragged 2D6&quot; towards the Lictor. 
If a model is dragged into base contact with the Lictor it must fight the creature in the close combat phase. The flesh hooks cannot drag a vehicle, dreadnought, terminator, or any model wit ha Strength or Toughness of 5 or more
If a Lictor runs or charges in the movement phase the flesh hooks allow it to move up or down vertical surfaces with no penalty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Devourer" id="e8de-6e38-d04b-86f0" hidden="false" page="56" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Squads that suffer 1 or more hits from this weapon must take a Leadership test for Fear. If they fail they will break as per Fear rules</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Barbed Strangler" id="6a62-0492-f309-667b" hidden="false" page="57" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Rol to hit as normal for shooting. If you miss, roll for scatter just like any other weapon with a blast marker.
A model wounded by this attack is killed regardless of how many wounds it has. Place the 3&quot; blast marker over the dead model. Roll a D6 for each model (including Tyranid models) and vehicles that is fully or partially under the template. On a 1,2 or 3 the model or vehicle escapes and can move and fight normally in its next turn. Otherwise roll 2D6 for each trapped model or vehicle. If the roll beats the model&apos;s Strength or Ram Value (for vehicles) it can play no further part in the battle at all. Saving throws, Toughness, wounds, and psychic powers cannot protect a model against the strangler if caught.
If the 2D6 is equal to or less than the Strength or Ram Value then the model breaks free and can move and fight as normal next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Venom Cannon" id="d7f2-06cb-94f0-6944" hidden="false" page="58" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Uses the Thudd Gunn Salvo template
If you miss, roll to scatter as normal then follow the steps in Tyranid Codex pg. 58</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hive Mind - Warrior" id="958b-9301-4992-1bc6" hidden="false" page="18" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>No other Tyranid unit within 12&quot; of the Tyranid Warrior need take any Leadership based test, they automatically pass. If an already broken unit is within 12&quot; of a Tyranid Warrior in the rally phase it will automatically rally.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hive Mind - Tyrant" id="fd95-6aac-8c28-27f0" hidden="false" page="18" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>No other Tyranid unit within 18&quot; of the Hive Tyrant need take any Leadership based test, they automatically pass. If an already broken unit is within 18&quot; of a Hive Tyrant in the rally phase it will automatically rally.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leadership" id="029d-d831-ac7e-79df" hidden="false" page="18" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Immune to all psychological factors. It cannot be affected by Fear, Terror, or any of the psychological factors in the Warhammer rulebook. Cannot be broken and does not have to take a Break test. Will automatically pass any Leadership-based test required to make.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Acute Senses" id="65ac-8308-b233-fe21" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Can spot hidden troops at twice it&apos;s Initiative distance in Inches</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Chameleon Scales" id="c8b0-8316-107e-ab44" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>All shots fired at a Lictor which did not move in its previous turn suffer a -1 to hit in addition to any other modifiers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hiding" id="0ed3-af90-812e-9646" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Lictors cannot be spotted when hidden, only detected. A scanner or Bionic Eye can only detect a hidden Lictor on a 4+. 
Can only be attacked by weapons with a template or blast marker, which still only hit them on a 4+ while they are Hidden.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Poison" id="d31a-8352-14b8-27d6" hidden="false" page="21" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Any close combat opponents wounded by a Lictor but not killed will suffer additional wounds from its poison at the end of the phase. Roll a D6, the poisoned model suffers 1 extra wound for each point the roll exceeds the model&apos;s Toughness by. Only make the roll on the turn the model is wounded.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immune to Psychology" id="8fb6-dd3b-4958-9616" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Immune to all psychology. Cannot be affected by fear, terror, or any of the psychological factors in the Warhammer rulebook. 
Still affected by Break tests like other troops</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leap" id="bf61-3098-5a1c-4ffc" hidden="false" page="25" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>When Hromagaunts run or charge they can make a 6&quot; leap in addition to their 12&quot; move. The leap can be up to 3&quot; in height and allows the Hormagaunt to ignore movement penalties for the terrain it&apos;s leaping over or into. 
May not leap over enemy models to attack models behind them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fly" id="8bd1-7d08-1366-3f60" hidden="false" page="24" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>May move over any terrain without penalty as they fly over it. Gargoyles cannot double their movement by running or charging. 
Gargoyles may leave the table during the movement phase and the models are removed. They may be placed anywhere on the battlefield in the Tyranid players next movement phase, even into close combat. May not make any other movement that turn but can shoot and fight normally</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Gargoyle Close Combat" id="fbec-a6f0-8fc5-c910" hidden="false" page="24" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Gargoyles get +1 WS when they charge or come down from the sky into combat.
Gargoyles can disengage from close combat without incurring any blows against them by flying high at the start of their next movement phase</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ripper Base" id="1148-bdf7-ec15-3ec7" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>A ripper swarm is 1 large oval base with multiple rippers on it. They count as a single model</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ripper Movement" id="0f69-584b-d495-f5a5" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>A Ripper base ignores all movement modifiers for terrain and can go up vertical surfaces at its normal movement rate</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ripper Combat" id="913c-dbe5-f8d6-aefb" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Enemy models outnumbering a Ripper base cannot count bonuses for multiple combat, so no +1 attack and +1 modifier for every attacker after the first</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ripper Terrain Consume" id="16ce-71ce-4f38-c854" hidden="false" page="23" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Ripper bases consume organic material as they move through terrain. Any organic terrain such as woods, plants, bushes etc. should be removed from the table as the Ripper swarm moves through it</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Haruspex Damage Table" id="4cfe-5676-3081-344e" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>1: Foot
2-4: Body
5-6: Arms*
Closest to attacker is hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Vehicle Targetting" id="7689-cdc9-5c99-988b" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Tyranid Vehicles are targeted as a Vehicle

Bolt Of Change, Force Dome, Hammer of Fury, Eldrich Storm, and Assail affect Tyranid vehicles  as vehicles. Vortex, Aura Of Decay, Aquiescence, Pink Fire Of Tzeench, Executioner, Kop Dis and Da Crunch work as normal. The Leadership test-based Powers (Domination, Smite, Scourging, Beam of Slaanesh, Pavane of Slaanesh and Storm Of Wrath) will apply to any Tyranid vehicle that is outside the range of a Hive Node (Hive Tyrant,Tyranid Warrior)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rampage" id="a5f3-6f1a-eaf0-e737" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Rampage: If it takes damage causing it to Rampage it must charge the nearest enemy model (character, squad, or vehicle) that it can reach, moving at the fastest possible speed towards the target. May not fire any weapons when Rampaging.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Haruspex Close Combat" id="58c7-a733-823f-0d61" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>Haruspex may ignore any infantry models in favour of vehicles when it charges. The Haruspex does not have to charge the closest target when it charges if it can not reach that target. The extra dice and +1 WS bonus for additional attackers does not apply against the Haruspex

The Ram Value is only used if the Haruspex is rammed or when making overrunn attacks

When a Tyranid vehicle rams or charges another vehicle, work out damage to the other vehicle as normal. For the Tyranid vehicle the location that actually touches the other vehicles is hit on a 4+ and other locations are hit on a 6+. Work out damage for any hit locations as normal

The Haruspex does not stop at the first enemy it comes into contact with. It keeps moving the full movement distance even if it ends within a squad. Any models touching the mandibles or within the area enclosed by the mandibles at the end of movement phase are attacked in close combat. If the Haruspex is moving too fast to end its movement in the midst of a squad, it will move through them and make an overrun attack as described in the Warhammer Rulebook (pg.78)

The Haruspex can attack multiple vehicles in the same turn, but does not get all of it&apos;s attacks for each vehicle. It must split it&apos;s attacks between them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Malefactor Damage Table" id="9cf1-b4ca-2d2f-bc3b" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>1: Foot
2-4: Body
5-6: Frag Spine Arms*
Closest to attacker is hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Malefactor Close Combat" id="e31b-10c9-e379-3a9a" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>The Malefactor uses its Ram Value for any damage inflicted by it in close combat. Because the Malefactor is so large, the extra dicem and +1 WS bonuses for additional attackers do not apply in any close combat with the Malefactor

When a Tyranid vehicle rams or charges another vehicle, work out damage to the other vehicle as normal. For the Tyranid vehicle the location that actually touches the other vehicles is hit on a 4+ and other locations are hit on a 6+. Work out damage for any hit locations as normal</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bio-Cannon" id="3bf3-4460-f4f2-4ed5" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>On the Tyranid player&apos;s turn (shooting phase) following a slime fungus round penetration, roll again (with a -1 modifier) on the same hit location Damage Table to represent the continuing action of the slime. Each subsequent turn repeat with an additional -1 modifier. If the modified result is ever 0 or less, the slime has become inactive and no further rolls are made.

For targeting purposes the Exocrine may ignore targets that have already been penetrated. The Exocrine relies on the destructive power of the slime fungus to finish off the enemy target, so it considers one penetrating hit enough and goes off to
hunt other vehicles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Exocrine Close Combat" id="2c96-bb20-c398-3ff8" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>The Exocrine uses its Ram Value for any damage inflicted by it in close combat. Because the Exocrine is so large, the extra dicem and +1 WS bonuses for additional attackers do not apply in any close combat with the Exocrine 

When a Tyranid vehicle rams or charges another vehicle, work out damage to the other vehicle as normal. For the Tyranid vehicle the location that actually touches the other vehicles is hit on a 4+ and other locations are hit on a 6+. Work out damage for any hit locations as normal</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Exocrine Damage Table" id="f08c-d0ce-7d01-7eba" hidden="false" publicationId="4740-6730-10c0-9b25">
      <description>1: Foot
2-4: Body
5-6: Bio-Cannon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Dactylis Damage Table" id="bfce-3f30-3007-7a02" hidden="false">
      <description>1: Foot
2-4: Body
5-6: Arms*
Closest to attacker is hit</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tyranid Dactylis - Nesting" id="3462-16bc-f280-2fd8" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Dactylis&apos; link with the HIve Mind is severed, it will Nest. While Nesting it will remain stationary and fire it&apos;s bile pods at the nearest enemy target, whether vehicle or infantry. The Dactylis is immune to psychology, and causes Fear</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bile Pods" id="9c2f-8b39-6eb3-6f7c" hidden="false">
      <description>Any models within 1&quot; of a pile pod blast marker will be splashed with corrosive bile on a D6 roll of 4+. Resolve splash hits with the normal stats of the weapon</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dactylis Close Combat" id="79aa-795d-9f48-e35d" hidden="false">
      <description>The Dactylis uses its Ram Value for any damage inflicted by it in close combat. Because the Dactylis is so large, the extra dice and +1 WS bonuses for additional attackers do not apply in any close combat with the Dactylis

When it rams or charges another vehicle, work out damage to the other vehicle as normal. For the Tyranid vehicle the location that actually touches the other vehicles is hit on a 4+ and other locations are hit on a 6+. Work out damage for any hit locations as normal.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
